+  "flatlay_insert_h2": "Can you check gold purity at home?",
+  "lifestyle_insert_h2": "How to read a BIS hallmark and HUID",
+  "more_reads_h2": "More gold jewellery buying guides",
+  "more_reads_html": "Continue with BlueStone guides to <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/best-gold-chain/\">choosing a gold chain</a>, <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/best-gold-rings-for-girls-in-india-buying-guide/\">choosing a gold ring</a>, <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/gold-bangles-design-2026/\">understanding gold bangle styles</a>, and <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/best-gold-coins-in-india/\">buying gold coins</a>.",
+  "tail_h2": "How to use this guide before buying",
+  "how_to_html": "Save the six step process, open the official BIS Care app before you visit the store, and compare the jewellery, HUID result, and invoice while they are together. If any detail remains uncertain, pause the purchase and ask for testing by a BIS recognized Assaying and Hallmarking Centre.",
+  "faq_h2": "Frequently Asked Questions about How to Check Gold Purity",
+  "section_leads": {
+    "How to check gold purity: a six step process": "A reliable purity check is a sequence, not a single trick. Start with the item itself, confirm the official identifiers, compare the paperwork, and escalate to a recognized laboratory when visual evidence is not enough.",
+    "Gold purity marks explained: karat and fineness": "Karat and fineness describe the declared proportion of gold in an alloy. The current <a href=\"https://www.bis.gov.in/hallmarking-overview/hallmarking-faqs/hallmarking-faq/?lang=en\">BIS hallmarking FAQ</a> lists six permitted gold grades under IS 1417:2016. The percentage column below is a direct conversion from fineness parts per thousand.",
+    "How to read a BIS hallmark and HUID": "According to the <a href=\"https://www.bis.gov.in/hallmarking-overview/hallmarking-faqs/hallmarking-faq/?lang=en\">BIS hallmarking FAQ</a>, a gold hallmark introduced with HUID contains the BIS logo, purity in karat and fineness, and a six character alphanumeric HUID. Read all three together.",
+    "How to verify HUID in the BIS Care app": "The <a href=\"https://www.bis.gov.in/bis-apps/?lang=en\">official BIS Care app page</a> lists Verify HUID as the feature for authenticating a hallmarked jewellery item. Verification is strongest when the engraving on the item, the app result, and the invoice all agree.",
+    "Can you check gold purity at home?": "You can perform safe screening at home, but you cannot establish fineness by colour, feel, or one simple household test. Use home checks to decide whether professional confirmation is needed, not to issue your own purity verdict.",
+    "When to use professional gold purity testing": "The <a href=\"https://www.bis.gov.in/hallmarking-overview/?lang=en\">BIS hallmarking overview</a> says consumers can get jewellery tested at a BIS recognized Assaying and Hallmarking Centre and receive an assay report. This is the appropriate next step for uncertainty or a dispute.",
